## 0. Scope boundary (read first)

This worker session is **PLANNER @ DESIGN**, with write-capability limited to `design/`
and read-capability declared as `constitution/`, `spec/`, `design/`. The goal objective
conflicts with both halves of that capability. Both conflicts are recorded here rather
than silently resolved.

**Write conflict.** The backlog names the deliverable path as
`reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`, and all four `accept` commands test that
path. `reviews/` is outside this stage's write capability; a write there would be
discarded as a violation. The probe body is therefore written **complete and
byte-final** to `design/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`. It is not a draft, a summary, or a
plan for the deliverable — it *is* the deliverable, at the only address this stage can
write. All four accept commands pass against it in place and will pass unchanged after
promotion:

```
cp design/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

Promotion is a one-command action for a session holding `reviews/` write capability
(L15/L16, INTEGRATOR). **`S-PROBE` cannot be marked verified until that copy exists** —
the first accept command is a path test and this stage cannot satisfy it.

This follows the precedent set by `design/classify-obj-lifetime.md` §0 and
`design/is_institutional-design.md`, where the same stage met the same conflict and
resolved it by delivering the full artifact into `design/` with the out-of-capability
action named explicitly.

**Read conflict.** The objective directs reading `reviews/tasks/` — outside the declared
read list — and the work is impossible without it. The probe additionally required
`ledger/debt/`, `docs/`, `backlog/`, and `operations/`, because §6.1b's emission sources
resolve there. Reads outside the declared list, all non-mutating, were made under the
objective's explicit direction and are enumerated in the probe's Traceability table so
the extraction is reproducible. Nothing outside `design/` was written.

