## 1. Goal restatement (acceptance surface)

Falsify or sustain SAEOS-1 §9/A8 — the specification's self-declared *"single largest
untested assumption"* — **before** any S1 code is written, per §10/D7's ratification of
S1 as "explicitly a falsification test".

The four acceptance commands (`backlog/SAKG-1-backlog.yaml`, node `S-PROBE`):

```
test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
rg -q '^verdict: (GO|NO-GO)$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md) -ge 3
rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

Status against `design/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md` (verified this session):

| Command | Result |
|---|---|
| path test | PASS at the `design/` address; PENDING at `reviews/spikes/` (§0) |
| `^verdict: (GO\|NO-GO)$` | **PASS** — `verdict: GO` at lines 7 and 388 |
| `^## goal: ` count ≥ 3 | **PASS** — exactly 3 (B0.0, B0.1, B0.2) |
