## 4. Data flow

```
① AUDIT     for each §6.1b named source: does the artifact exist?
              └─▶ 5 of 6 absent. Re-point at the sources that do exist. (F1)

② SELECT    3 goals with status=Sealed in the Atlas → B0.0, B0.1, B0.2
              └─▶ these are the backlog's named examples AND the corpus's
                  best-documented goals ⇒ the result is a LOWER BOUND on loss

③ ENUMERATE fix N = 41 fields/goal before looking at any artifact
              └─▶ prevents denominator drift

④ EXTRACT   per (goal × node_type × field): locate → score → record basis
              └─▶ 123 scored rows

⑤ AGGREGATE per-goal loss ─┐
            per-family loss ┼─▶ headline loss_ratio = 0.134
                            ┘

⑥ INTERPRET separate corpus-completeness loss from schema-viability loss
              └─▶ all 7 findings are completeness ⇒ fixable at the source
              └─▶ VERDICT: GO, conditional on C1..C7

⑦ FALSIFY   name the observation that would flip the verdict
              └─▶ re-probe 3 goals with NO debt entry; loss > 0.35 ⇒ NO-GO
```

Step ⑥ is the design's load-bearing judgment and the one a reviewer should attack first.
It is defended in §7 under *Adversarial*.

