## 5. State machines

### 5.1 Node epistemic state (SAEOS-1 §4.2) — what S1 may and may not drive

```
                    ┌───────────────┐
    §6.1b ingest ──▶│   candidate   │  every extracted node lands here
                    └───┬───────┬───┘
       evidence binding │       │ falsifier observed
       (×5: NEVER a     │       │
        frequency       ▼       ▼
        threshold) ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────┐
                   │ canonical│ │ refuted  │  RETAINED — a refuted
                   └────┬─────┘ └──────────┘  decision is high-value (✓1)
                        │  superseded by a later decision
                        ▼
                   ┌────────────┐
                   │ superseded │   nothing is ever deleted (§4.2)
                   └────────────┘
```

**S1's authority stops at `candidate`.** The probe found that all three goals are `Sealed`
in PAEOS and carry passing evidence — which is *tempting* grounds to ingest them straight to
`canonical`. §4.2's ×5 invariant forbids it: promotion requires an evidence **binding**, and
Finding F5 shows the binding (`artifact_hash`/`env_hash`) does not exist for pre-B0.7 goals.
**The historical corpus is therefore structurally stuck at `candidate`**, and §5.1 rule 4
defaults queries to `[canonical]`. Consequence, and a direct input to `G-S1-GO`: *S2 will
return nothing from the historical corpus unless the caller opts into `status: [candidate]`.*

This is a real interaction between F5 and §5.1 that neither section states alone.

### 5.2 Probe verdict state machine

```
   ┌────────────┐  5 of 6 sources absent   ┌──────────────────┐
   │ source     │─────────────────────────▶│ re-point sources │
   │ audit      │                          │ (F1)             │
   └────────────┘                          └────────┬─────────┘
                                                    ▼
   ┌──────────────┐   loss > 0.35 on the      ┌──────────────┐
   │ score 3      │   sampled goals           │   NO-GO      │
   │ sealed goals │──────────────────────────▶│ §7 falsifier │
   └──────┬───────┘                           │ fires; spec  │
          │ loss ≤ 0.35                       │ reverted     │
          ▼                                   └──────────────┘
   ┌──────────────────┐
   │ classify losses  │  schema-viability loss ⇒ NO-GO
   │ (step ⑥)         │  completeness loss     ⇒ GO + conditions
   └──────┬───────────┘
          │ all 7 findings = completeness
          ▼
   ┌──────────────┐        ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
   │ GO           │───────▶│ G-S1-GO (founder A4)             │
   │ + C1..C7     │        │ PROCEED ─▶ F-BUNDLE, F-ENVELOPE  │
   └──────────────┘        │ REVERT  ─▶ SAEOS-1 §7 falsifier  │
                           └──────────────────────────────────┘
```

The 0.35 threshold is not in the spec — it is this design's proposal, chosen so that the
NO-GO re-test (three goals with no debt entry) has a pre-declared bar rather than a
post-hoc one. The founder may set it elsewhere at `G-S1-GO`.

