## 9. Handoff

**To INTEGRATOR (L15/L16), one command:**

```
cp design/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

Then all four `S-PROBE` accept commands pass and the node may be marked verified.

**To `G-S1-GO` (FOUNDER, A4).** Two questions, in priority order:

1. **A7** — does §8's "round-trip is lossless" mean bundle→store→bundle (verdict GO) or
   artifact→bundle (verdict NO-GO at any loss > 0)? This single ruling determines the gate.
2. **A2** — do the absent artifact classes (ADR/decision-graph, L06 matrices, scar corpus)
   exist outside this workspace? A yes materially improves the loss ratio and softens F1/F4.

**To `F-BUNDLE` (PLANNER).** Conditions C1, C2, C3, C7; the corrected source list (§2) and
field-resolution table (§3.2) are drop-in inputs.

**To `F-ENVELOPE` (PLANNER).** Conditions C4, C5, C6 — `recomputed_at_ingest` tagging,
nullable `run_id`, and a closed coordinate dimension set.

**To `F-EXTRACT-FIX` (PLANNER).** The three per-goal tables are the hand-extraction targets
its golden fixtures must encode; §5.1 explains why fixtures must assert `status: candidate`
and never `canonical`. Its two adversarial cases are already characterised by this probe:
"a goal whose L06 matrix is absent" is **every goal**, and the debt-free goal is the NO-GO
re-test population.

